# This file describes files and paths that should not be tracked by Git version control
# https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore
#
# This repository contains the collaboration library and its tooling and nothing else.
# The s&box test project this library was developed in (Assets, Code, ProjectSettings,
# the project's .sbproj) shares the folder for development but is not published, so the
# top level below is a whitelist: only the library, Tools/, and this repository's own
# files are ever added. Local session data, the relay access key, editor caches and
# build output can therefore never enter the repository by accident.

# Top level: track only the library, its tooling, and the repository's own files.
/*
!/Libraries
!/Tools
!/README.md
!/PUBLISHING.md
!/LICENSE
!/.gitignore

# Auto-generated code editor files (at any depth)
.vs/
.vscode/
obj/
bin/
Properties/
*.csproj
!Tools/**/*.csproj
*launchSettings.json
*.sln
*.slnx

# Auto-generated asset related files (at any depth)
.sbox/
*.generated.*
*.*_c
!*.shader_c
*.los
*.vpk

# Session data, local secrets and disposable test copies (at any depth)
.collaboration/
.research/
TestResults/
Exports/

# Relay deployment secrets (the access key). Only .env.example is tracked.
Tools/Relay/.env

# Cloudflare Worker relay: dependencies, local dev state and local secrets. Only the
# source, the config and the lock file are tracked.
Tools/RelayWorker/node_modules/
Tools/RelayWorker/.wrangler/
Tools/RelayWorker/tmp/
Tools/RelayWorker/.dev.vars
